00:09:28.233 --> 00:09:29.668
[ Laughter ]
Right?

00:09:29.668 --> 00:09:31.670
-Are you gonna get in trouble
for doing this?

00:09:31.670 --> 00:09:34.072
-Yes. Of course I am.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:34.072 --> 00:09:35.541
I can't even go anywhere
with the costume.

00:09:35.541 --> 00:09:38.210
They have, like, a person --
like, a person who travels

00:09:38.210 --> 00:09:40.012
with the costume, and the helmet
comes in its own thing,

00:09:40.012 --> 00:09:41.547
and the person
travels with the helmet.

00:09:41.547 --> 00:09:42.715
They're like,
"Here's the costume,

00:09:42.715 --> 00:09:44.650
and then here's the helmet.
Take care of it."

00:09:44.650 --> 00:09:46.452
-I was gonna say --
I was gonna say to you --

00:09:46.452 --> 00:09:48.086
I was gonna make fun of you and
go like, "Oh, do you have

00:09:48.086 --> 00:09:49.321
a security guard?"
-No. You made fun of me enough.

00:09:49.321 --> 00:09:50.689
-Thank you.
-Yeah.

00:09:50.689 --> 00:09:52.625
I was gonna say, do you have
a security guard with you?

00:09:52.625 --> 00:09:54.827
You're John Cena.
You are your own security guard.

00:09:54.827 --> 00:09:56.028
-No, it's for the helmet.
It's for the helmet.

00:09:56.028 --> 00:09:58.163
-It's for the helmet.
-That is now not mine

00:09:58.163 --> 00:10:00.399
and wasn't mine in the first
place but now, somehow, you own.

00:10:00.399 --> 00:10:02.467
[ Laughter ]
-I think it's pretty cool.

00:10:02.467 --> 00:10:04.503
I might just do it and just
host the show with it on.

00:10:04.503 --> 00:10:06.605
-It's actually really cool,
because the audience

00:10:06.605 --> 00:10:09.408
gets to see themselves on TV!
-That's right.

00:10:09.408 --> 00:10:12.912
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:12.912 --> 00:10:14.680
I want to --

00:10:14.680 --> 00:10:16.415
-That's not frosted tips,
but it'll do.

00:10:16.415 --> 00:10:17.983
-[ Laughs ]
-We're kind of all winners here.

00:10:17.983 --> 00:10:20.085
-That's the next bet.
We've never talked --

00:10:20.085 --> 00:10:21.720
You've been on the show,
I want to say,

00:10:21.720 --> 00:10:23.321
it's almost 15 times now.

00:10:23.321 --> 00:10:25.057
We've known each other
a long time, yeah.

00:10:25.057 --> 00:10:26.292
And we've never talked
about this --

00:10:26.292 --> 00:10:27.493
-Thank you, guys.
I appreciate that.

00:10:27.493 --> 00:10:28.527
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:28.527 --> 00:10:30.329
-No, we add
the applause in later.

00:10:30.329 --> 00:10:32.230
We add the applause in later.
-Okay, cool.

00:10:32.230 --> 00:10:34.100
-We do that to the monologue,
as well.

00:10:34.100 --> 00:10:36.635
We've had you --
You've been a guest 15 times.

00:10:36.635 --> 00:10:39.471
We've never referenced
the "You can't see me" move.

00:10:39.471 --> 00:10:42.108
-Yeah!
-Of where -- Like, what --

00:10:42.108 --> 00:10:44.576
Like, what is the back story?
-Okay. So, for those of you

00:10:44.576 --> 00:10:47.245
who don't know,
get the damn Internet!

00:10:47.245 --> 00:10:49.648
-[ Laughs ] Yeah!
Of course.

00:10:49.648 --> 00:10:52.051
-I am -- I became a superhero
long before donning

00:10:52.051 --> 00:10:53.986
the Peacemaker costume.

00:10:53.986 --> 00:10:57.522
I developed a special maneuver
in the WWE,

00:10:57.522 --> 00:10:59.225
called the "You can't see me,"
in which I put my hand

00:10:59.225 --> 00:11:02.161
in front of my face and say,
"You can't see me."

00:11:02.161 --> 00:11:04.997
And the reason I did this is,
because while we were making

00:11:04.997 --> 00:11:07.799
the album
to which my theme music is on,

00:11:07.799 --> 00:11:12.137
my younger brother, Sean,
was always our litmus test.

00:11:12.137 --> 00:11:13.972
He kind of liked the same music,
and he would never go

00:11:13.972 --> 00:11:15.674
to the studio with us, so we'd
come home with our tracks,

00:11:15.674 --> 00:11:17.576
and we'd play it for him,
and he was ruthless, man.

00:11:17.576 --> 00:11:20.479
He would never be satisfied
with any song.

00:11:20.479 --> 00:11:23.649
And he heard, "The Time is Now"
and just did this dance

00:11:23.649 --> 00:11:26.485
that Tony Yayo did
in of the G-Unit videos.

00:11:26.485 --> 00:11:29.054
It was like he put his hand
over his head and just kind of,

00:11:29.054 --> 00:11:30.689
like, bobbed his head like that.

00:11:30.689 --> 00:11:32.257
-Oh, yeah,
I kind of remember that.

00:11:32.257 --> 00:11:33.325
-And I was like,
"Man, what are you doing?

00:11:33.325 --> 00:11:34.826
That looked like --
is ridiculous."

00:11:34.826 --> 00:11:36.862
He's like, "No, no, man.
This is some Tony Yayo dancing,

00:11:36.862 --> 00:11:38.063
doing his thing."

00:11:38.063 --> 00:11:40.166
And I'm like,
"I'll do it on TV."

00:11:40.166 --> 00:11:42.368
And he's like,
"I dare you to do it on TV."

00:11:42.368 --> 00:11:43.803
[ Laughter ]

00:11:43.803 --> 00:11:46.372
Little did he know,
I'll do this on TV, so...

00:11:46.372 --> 00:11:48.007
[ Laughter ]

00:11:48.007 --> 00:11:49.708
It was before then.
-Don't dare John Cena.

00:11:49.708 --> 00:11:54.847
-So, basically -- basically,
on a dare, by absolute chance,

00:11:54.847 --> 00:11:57.249
I went out there, and I figured
this wasn't visible enough,

00:11:57.249 --> 00:12:00.986
so I wanted to do this.
And the term "You can't see me"

00:12:00.986 --> 00:12:02.988
is, like, "Well, you're not
even on my level."

00:12:02.988 --> 00:12:06.559
And then, like, years later,
it just overcame

00:12:06.559 --> 00:12:09.228
the meme culture,
and now literally I'm invisible.

00:12:09.228 --> 00:12:11.363
People are like,
"Why is Jimmy Fallon

00:12:11.363 --> 00:12:13.532
talking to an empty chair?"
Like, so many people

00:12:13.532 --> 00:12:15.167
are gonna say that.
-Yeah, they really are.

00:12:15.167 --> 00:12:17.002
-So I'm invisible now.
-You are invisible.

00:12:17.002 --> 00:12:18.069
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:18.069 --> 00:12:21.440
-On a dare!
By accident!

00:12:21.440 --> 00:12:23.709
-I want to talk about
"Peacemaker."

00:12:23.709 --> 00:12:25.277
Gosh, it's funny.
-Thank you.

00:12:25.277 --> 00:12:27.580
-It is --
It's insane, as well.

00:12:27.580 --> 00:12:31.016
-Thank you!
-Is it you or is it James Gunn

00:12:31.016 --> 00:12:32.918
or is it a combo platter
of both?

00:12:32.918 --> 00:12:35.854
-It's James Gunn, for sure.
He's such an unbelievably

00:12:35.854 --> 00:12:38.590
gifted story teller,
and I think his ability

00:12:38.590 --> 00:12:42.293
to just put together
a great squad -- pun intended.

00:12:42.293 --> 00:12:45.030
But the mind of James Gunn is --
-He wrote all of these?

00:12:45.030 --> 00:12:46.531
-All of these, yes.

00:12:46.531 --> 00:12:48.033
-When does he have time
to do all this stuff?

00:12:48.033 --> 00:12:50.736
-Well, so when we all
really got locked down,

00:12:50.736 --> 00:12:52.537
if you saw
"The Suicide Squad" --

00:12:52.537 --> 00:12:53.705
-Yeah.
-You know, there's a --

00:12:53.705 --> 00:12:55.540
[ Cheers and applause ]
Thank you.

00:12:55.540 --> 00:12:59.244
But Peacemaker's future
is very questionable.

00:12:59.244 --> 00:13:01.780
And he called me up
in the middle of lockdown.

00:13:01.780 --> 00:13:04.283
He's like, "Hey, man, I want to
do a series on Peacemaker."

00:13:04.283 --> 00:13:06.252
I said, "Hey, man,
isn't Peacemaker dead?"

00:13:06.252 --> 00:13:07.586
[ Laughter ]

00:13:07.586 --> 00:13:09.888
And he was like, "No, no,
I got it taken care of."

00:13:09.888 --> 00:13:11.457
I said, "Okay. I'm in.
No problem."

00:13:11.457 --> 00:13:13.959
And I just let him go to work,
and he wrote eight episodes

00:13:13.959 --> 00:13:16.027
in eight weeks,
and then we filmed

00:13:16.027 --> 00:13:17.196
very shortly after that.

00:13:17.196 --> 00:13:19.864
-I will just say this.
Here's where you got me.

00:13:19.864 --> 00:13:22.935
The opening theme song.
-The big dance number.

00:13:22.935 --> 00:13:26.438
-Dude, he's not kidding.
-Dare you to skip the intro.

00:13:26.438 --> 00:13:28.307
[ Laughter ]

00:13:28.307 --> 00:13:30.075
-You did something
that we've been wanting to do

00:13:30.075 --> 00:13:33.245
is bring back the TV
kind of theme-song intro.

00:13:33.245 --> 00:13:35.214
And you come out --
-Not quite "Too Many Cooks,"

00:13:35.214 --> 00:13:36.382
but, I mean, it's good.

00:13:36.382 --> 00:13:38.917
-It is like solid gold
is what I would call it.

00:13:38.917 --> 00:13:40.552
Like the show, "Solid Gold."
[ Laughter ]

00:13:40.552 --> 00:13:44.156
It is like you come out,
full on choreographed dancing.

00:13:44.156 --> 00:13:45.891
Full on --
Serious face, by the way.

00:13:45.891 --> 00:13:49.094
-Yeah. I mean, you'll all
see it, I hope, on HBO Max.

00:13:49.094 --> 00:13:51.196
[ Cheers and applause ]
You'll all see it?

00:13:51.196 --> 00:13:52.931
-Every cast member --

00:13:52.931 --> 00:13:55.601
Every cast member comes out
and introduces themselves,

00:13:55.601 --> 00:13:58.303
and they're all dancing, too,
and doing these --

00:13:58.303 --> 00:14:00.772
It's so silly, I go,
"Oh, my gosh.

00:14:00.772 --> 00:14:03.108
He crushed it already."
Before the show even starts.

00:14:03.108 --> 00:14:06.044
Everything's funny.
Your sidekick, your pet --

00:14:06.044 --> 00:14:08.847
-The bald eagle -- Eagly.
[ Laughter ]

00:14:08.847 --> 00:14:11.049
-His name is Eagly.
-Yeah, it is Eagly.

00:14:11.049 --> 00:14:13.018
Yeah, it is Eagly.
My eagle's name is Eagly.

00:14:13.018 --> 00:14:14.687
[ Laughter ]

